    choose: [['We have agreed (on / at) a name.', 'on'], ['I will be responsible (for / of) the menu.', 'for'], ['Nao will (contact / contacted) local artists.', 'contact'], ['Ren will prepare the promotional (materials / materially).', 'materials'], ['Please send the draft (by / since) Friday.', 'by'], ['Check the date before (posting / post) it.', 'posting']],
    choices: [['"Emma creates the identity; Ren makes the poster." Who creates the identity?', 'Ren', 'Emma', 'B'], ['"Send the first ideas by Wednesday evening." What is Wednesday evening?', 'The deadline for first ideas', 'The confirmed market opening', 'A'], ['"Check the date before posting." What comes first?', 'Publish the unchecked poster.', 'Check the date.', 'B'], ['Which reply confirms a task clearly?', 'I will plan the menu and send my ideas by Wednesday.', 'Someone will probably do something.', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: ['You are Emma. Your tutor reads Claire\'s new handover message, then plays Ren. The project now has an approved logo. Explain what Ren needs to prepare and what must happen before publication.', 'あなたはエマ役です。講師はクレアの新しい引き継ぎの連絡を読んでから、レン役になります。ロゴは承認されました。レンが用意するものと、公開前に必要なことを説明しましょう。'], task: ['Listen for the item, deadline, design version and final check. Confirm the sequence with Ren and correct the idea that a completed draft can be posted immediately.', '作るもの、期限、使うデザイン、最後の確認を聞き取りましょう。レンと順序を確認し、下書きができればすぐ公開できるという思い込みを訂正しましょう。'], roles: ['Ren', 'Emma'], text: '<p>Ren, please prepare the online poster using Emma\'s approved logo. Send the draft to Emma by Friday at four. Emma will check the market date and opening hours. Do not post it until she confirms those details. I will share the final version with the artists after that.</p>', lines: ['Emma, what does Claire want me to prepare?', 'Which logo should I use?', 'When should I send you the draft?', 'What will you check before I post it?', 'If I finish early, can I publish without waiting?', 'Who will share the final version with the artists?'], evidence: 'Online poster, approved logo, Friday4 draft to Emma, market date/hours check, wait for confirmation, Claire shares final with artists. Wednesday first-ideas deadline belongs to earlier Apply message, not this new draft. Replay a requested sentence; assess listening separately from spoken grammar.', useful: ['She asked you to ...', 'Use the approved ...', 'The draft is due by ...', 'I will check ...', 'Please wait until ...', 'After that, Claire will ...'] },
