    trivia: ['A "draft" is an unfinished version open to changes. "Final" describes a version intended to be complete. In a team, saying "I finished my draft" does not necessarily mean "You can publish it."', 'draft は修正の余地がある下書き、final は完成版として扱う版です。チームで「下書きができた」と言っても、「公開してよい」という意味とは限りません。'], triviaQuestion: ['Does finishing a draft automatically give permission to publish?', 'No. The team may still need a final check.'],
